1590:<p></p><h2 style="text-align: justify; "><span>Shrimati Panadevi Morijawala Rajkiya Kanya Mahavidyalaya, Kotputli was established in 1997. By the great inspiration of the late freedom fighter and former&nbsp;MLA Shri&nbsp;Mukti Lal Modi.&nbsp;The college building was constructed by 'Bhamashah'&nbsp; Shri. Laxmi Narayan Morijawala. By the efforts of former&nbsp;MLA and parliamentary Secretary Shri&nbsp;Ram Swaroop Kasana, Science faculty building was&nbsp;constructed by the state Government.&nbsp;Science faculty was&nbsp;started in the college from the session 2010-11 onwards.&nbsp;</span></h2>    <p><span>In 1997 there were only 107 girls, but in the current academic session 1857 girls are studying in the college. &nbsp;Library, Games &amp; Sports, NSS, Rangering, Women Cell, Youth Development Centre, Planning Form, Laboratory facilities are available in the college. The college is recognized under 2 f and 12 b&nbsp;act of UGC and is a &nbsp;RUSA Beneficiary Institute.</span></p>    <p><span><strong>VISION</strong></span></p>    <p><span>To make our institution a centre of Excellence in the field of higher education for girls by ensuring high quality of teaching-learning experience achieved through a combination of</span></p>    <ul>  	<li><span>Excellent academic training.·</span></li>  	<li><span>Self-confidence building among girls and&nbsp;fostering global competencies.·</span></li>  	<li><span>Inculcation of values such as justice, equality and team work.·</span></li>  	<li><span>Capacity building of the staff·</span></li>  </ul>    <p><span>We aim to inculcate a feeling of social responsibility among students by training them in social entrepreneurship so that they are able to bring a societal change by economic upliftment of people in their neighborhood and villages, thereby contributing to the National development.</span></p>    <p><span>&nbsp;<strong>MISSION</strong></span></p>    <p><span>The mission statement of our college defines the action plan and determines the specific tasks for achieving the vision.</span></p>    <ul>  	<li><span>To impart excellent academic training to the students using innovative methods.·</span></li>  	<li><span>To inculcate self-confidence for achieving overall success in life.·</span></li>  	<li><span>Training the students in soft skills, community service and nation building.·</span></li>  	<li><span>Training in entrepreneurship with special emphasis on social entrepreneurship.·</span></li>  	<li><span>To make students aware of higher education· &amp; best career opportunities.</span></li>  	<li><span>To increase the reach of higher education to the weaker sections of the society·</span></li>  	<li><span>To encourage the use of IT in teaching-learning, administration· &amp; communication.</span></li>  </ul>    <p>&nbsp;</p>    <p><span>&nbsp;<strong>OBJECTIVES</strong></span></p>    <ul>  	<li><span>Impart Quality education to excel in university examination and avail best career opportunities.</span></li>  	<li><span>Conducting camps, excursions, seminars, training sessions and awareness programs.·</span></li>  	<li><span>To develop analytical skills, soft skills, research· &amp; scientific temperament &amp; rational approach.</span></li>  	<li><span>Teach latest management principles such as time management, stress management etc.</span></li>  	<li><span>Introduce Quality Concepts to students and staff to increase efficiency and·effectiveness.</span></li>  	<li><span>To Increase awareness about· &amp; give benefit of the various scholarship schemes of the government .</span></li>  	<li><span>Inspire students to be a role-model· &amp; torch-bearer to bring about positive societal change by economic &amp; social up-liftment.</span></li>  	<li><span>Focus on capacity building of teaching and non-teaching staff.·</span></li>  </ul>    <p><span><strong><u>History</u></strong></span></p>    <p><span><strong>Our Principals</strong></span></p>    <table border="1" cellpadding="0" cellsp